#+title: First-playable acceptance record

* Brief and boundary
Record the player loop, perspective, target device and first win/loss condition.
List the engine pin, selected template and exact hooks used. Separate base
behavior from the level, collision, UI and rules implemented by the game.

* Ownership and timing
Record who owns the host, game states, asset references and persistent objects.
Identify which callback advances simulation and who polls input/updates audio.
State how pause, restart and teardown affect each owner.

* Example acceptance case
Given a player without a key at a locked exit, interaction keeps the exit locked.
After a successful pickup, interaction opens the exit exactly once. Restart
restores the locked exit and initial player state. Replace this concrete scenario
with the chosen game's first loop and enumerate its failure boundaries.

* Verification record
Record exact build/test commands, fixtures/seeds, observed results and skips.
Separate source inspection, headless tests and real display/audio observations.
Include launch command, controls, data-root policy and known unfinished behavior.
